The attached image, Figure 2 (A) and (B), illustrates the physical characteristics of Nano-11 nanoparticles. The transmission electron microscopy (TEM) image (A) shows spherical particles with an irregular, cauliflower-like appearance, mostly appearing as single units or small pairs, with a 50 nm scale bar. The dynamic light scattering (DLS) distribution (B) indicates a narrow particle size range, with the diameter of Nano-11 predominantly between 70 and 80 nm, which the study highlights as optimal for efficient uptake by dendritic cells and for their role as an effective vaccine adjuvant.